Band Description

Kaval Tripwire is a four-member acoustic-electronic ensemble built around the rule that every programmed rhythm must remain subordinate to live breath.

Elena Stoyanova — kaval, modal lead lines, overblown harmonics, breath cues, phrase-length control.
Malik Velez — Jersey-club drums, low bass pulses, live mutes, triplet variation, structural resets.
Iva Koleva — prepared harp, muted strings, papery attacks, pitch shadows, dry harmonic punctuation.
Petar Marinov — baritone horn, breath-led pedals, compact fifths, half-valve smears, low-register handoffs.

There is no conventional frontperson. Elena governs phrase duration, Malik governs recoil and silence, Iva governs decay, and Petar governs low acoustic pressure. Live transitions are cued by visible inhalations, kaval finger lifts, one specific harp mute, or heel impacts rather than backing-track markers.

